 60TI c  Compiled (unevaluated) data set from 2011Da08:                         
 60TI2c  Phys Rev C 83, 054312 (2011)                                           
 60TI c  Compiled by M. Birch and B. Singh (McMaster); May 19 {I2011}.          
 60TI c  {+60}Ti produced in the fragmentation of 57.8 MeV/nucleon {+86}Kr      
 60TI2c  beam impinged on 50 mg/cm{+2} thick tantalum target using LISE-2000    
 60TI3c  spectrometer at GANIL facility. Detector system included a             
 60TI4c  three-element Si-detector telescope containing a double-sided          
 60TI5c  silicon-strip detector (DSSSD) backed by a Si(Li) detector and         
 60TI6c  surrounded by four clover type EXOGAM Ge detectors. Product            
 60TI7c  identified by mass, atomic number, charge, energy loss and time of     
 60TI8c  flight. Measured half-life.                                            
 60TI  L 0              0+               22.4 MS   25                           
 60TI cL T$ based on time correlation between implantation and |b-ray events    
 60TI2cL in the DSSSD. Fitting procedure included five parameters: |b-detection 
 60TI3cL efficiency, background rate, mother, daughter and granddaughter        
 60TI4cL half-lives (2011Da08)                                                  
                                                                                
